# Description: Select EF.DIR, the card's built-in application directory file.
# Category: selection
#
# WHAT THIS DOES
# EF.DIR is a standard file that lists the applications (AIDs) available on
# the card. This script only SELECTS the file; it does not read it yet. The
# companion script read_ef_dir selects EF.DIR and then reads its contents.
# Nothing on the card is modified.
#
# THE COMMAND, BYTE BY BYTE
#   00     class byte: standard interindustry commands
#   A4     instruction: SELECT FILE
#   02     P1 = 2: select an elementary file (EF) by file identifier
#   00     P2 = 0: first or only occurrence, no control info requested
#   02     Lc: exactly 2 data bytes follow
#   2F 00  file identifier reserved for EF.DIR by the ISO 7816-4 standard
#
# WHAT YOU SHOULD SEE
#   SW 90 00 or 61 XX    EF.DIR is now the currently selected file
#   SW 6A 82             the card has no EF.DIR under the current directory
#
# This command does not write anything to the card.
00 A4 02 00 02 2F 00
